# RealKevbase hints — always-on rules. Details: AGENTS.md, scripts/README.md.

Stack: .NET 10 minimal API (`src/RealKevbase.Api`) + Core library, React 19 + Vite +
MUI SPA (`src/realkevbase-web`). `zz_tp/` is the vendored PDF generator with its own
rules (`zz_tp/AGENTS.md`): never run `tpr`, use `zz_tp/scripts/render-check.sh`.

- Products are C# seed data in `Core/Services/InMemoryProductCatalog.cs`. Add or change
  one with `python3 scripts/sync-catalog.py` (writes the DB row, uploads the PDF,
  publishes images). Never edit only one of the three sides.
- Shop copy is `zz_tp/documents/<listing>/listing.txt` — name is the first pipe
  segment, the `DESCRIPTION` block is the card copy. Edit the file, not the C#.
- Ship with `./scripts/deploy.sh --yes` after `dotnet build` and `npm run build` pass;
  deploy refuses while `sync-catalog.py` reports drift.
- Never copy `zz_tp/projects.db` over `src/RealKevbase.Api/Data/projects.db` — the
  shipped copy carries the titles and the source has no `title` column.
- No secrets in code, docs or commits: Stripe, blob storage and Azure Email come from
  environment variables or App Service settings.
- The browser only ever sees `/api/...` URLs; blob names, storage paths and SAS links
  stay server-side.
- Public C# members keep XML docs; keep every diff inside the task's scope.
- Navigate with `lua scripts/repo-intel.lua overview|symbol <Name>|deps <X>` and `rg`
  before opening whole files.
